    <h1>Noise Pollution Concerns</h1>
    
    <p>Data centers operate 24/7, creating a constant low-frequency hum from industrial cooling fans and backup generators. Unlike intermittent noise, this persistent sound can have significant impacts on residential health.</p>

    <div class="resource-box">
        <h3>Key Findings from EESI:</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Constant Exposure:</strong> Constant noise above 65 decibels is linked to increased blood pressure and stress.</li>
            <li><strong>Low-Frequency Vibration:</strong> The "hum" can travel through walls and windows, making it difficult to mitigate with standard home insulation.</li>
            <li><strong>Sleep Disturbance:</strong> Ongoing nighttime noise is a leading cause of sleep deprivation in communities near industrial zones.</li>
        </ul>
        
